menu "device_esp32s3_gpio"

    config ESP32S3_GPIO_PWM_DEFAULT_FREQ_HZ
        int "PWM frequency before one is set (Hz)"
        range 5 5000000
        default 1000
        help
          The frequency a PWM pin starts at when its duty is written before
          any frequency. Pins share LEDC timers by frequency, so the pins left
          at this default use one timer between them.

    config ESP32S3_GPIO_PWM_TIMER_MASK
        hex "LEDC timers PWM pins may use (bit per timer)"
        range 0x1 0xF
        default 0xF
        help
          Bit n set: LEDC timer n is for PWM pins (ESP32-S3: timers 0-3).
          Clear the bits of the timers another LEDC user needs (a buzzer, an
          LCD backlight, a camera clock). Each timer runs one PWM frequency,
          so this is also the number of frequencies at once. Other LEDC users
          must use the APB clock too: on the ESP32-S3 every LEDC timer shares
          one clock source.

    config ESP32S3_GPIO_PWM_CHANNEL_MASK
        hex "LEDC channels PWM pins may use (bit per channel)"
        range 0x1 0xFF
        default 0xFF
        help
          Bit n set: LEDC channel n is for PWM pins (ESP32-S3: channels 0-7).
          One channel per PWM pin, so this is also the number of pins that
          run PWM at once. Clear the bits of the channels another LEDC user
          needs.

    config ESP32S3_GPIO_DEBOUNCE_MS
        int "Debounce time of pin interrupts (ms)"
        range 1 1000
        default 50
        help
          A pin armed by INTR with debounce = 1 ignores the edges that come
          sooner than this after the last one it published. A pin armed with
          debounce = 0 (a chip's alert line) publishes every edge.

    config ESP32S3_GPIO_ADC_TASK_STACK
        int "Stack of the ADC task (bytes)"
        range 2048 16384
        default 4096
        help
          The task that reads the conversion of the pins in ADC mode, filters
          it and raises their thresholds. Its frame buffer (256 B) is on this
          stack.

    config ESP32S3_GPIO_ADC_TASK_PRIO
        int "Priority of the ADC task"
        range 1 24
        default 5
        help
          Below the tasks that run commands and events: the readings are
          filtered, so a late frame costs nothing but its delay.

endmenu
